---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../../styles/docs.css";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Base
	title="Live sidebar | Actual Budget Tweaks"
	description="Account groups, shortcuts, layouts and live balances in the Actual Budget Tweaks sidebar."
>
	<main class="docs center">
		<header class="docs__header stack stack--sm">
			<a href="/guides" class="docs__back">Back to guides</a>
			<h1>Live sidebar</h1>
			<p class="docs__lead">
				The Live sidebar replaces Actual's sidebar with one that has live balances, account groups,
				search and shortcuts. Turning it off brings Actual's sidebar back.
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Pin a shortcut</h2>
			<p>
				Click the dashed tile under the navigation links. Sidebar settings opens on its Shortcuts tab.
				Pick an item on the right to pin it.
			</p>
			<div class="docs__stage docs__stage--dialog">
			<img
				src={`${base}images/guides/sidebar-shortcuts.png`}
				width="640"
				height="620"
				alt="The Shortcuts tab of Sidebar settings, with pinned tiles on the left and the items you can add on the right"
			/>
			</div>
			<p>
				Drag a tile to rearrange it, in the sidebar or on this tab. Tiles stay on the rows you put
				them on. To remove one, hover it on this tab.
			</p>
			<p>
				Clicking a tool tile opens the tool in a window you can drag by its title bar. Clicking the
				tile again closes it.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Group your accounts</h2>
			<p>
				Open the <a href="/guides/command-palette">command palette</a>, choose
				<strong>Sidebar settings</strong> and go to the Groups tab. Add a group under On budget or Off
				budget.
			</p>
			<div class="docs__stage docs__stage--dialog">
			<img
				src={`${base}images/guides/sidebar-groups.png`}
				width="640"
				height="315"
				alt="The Groups tab of Sidebar settings with a Cash group holding two accounts"
			/>
			</div>
			<p>
				In the sidebar, drag an account onto a group to move it there. Right-click a group to rename
				or remove it. Removing a group keeps its accounts. Turn on Account Group Totals to show each
				group's combined balance.
			</p>
			<p>
				On versions of Actual with account groups, the sidebar uses Actual's groups. On older
				versions, ABT keeps its own.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Choose a layout</h2>
			<p>
				Change the layout on the General tab of Sidebar settings. Split is the default, with the
				navigation on an icon bar so more of the width goes to accounts.
			</p>
			<div class="docs__stage docs__stage--pair">
				<figure>
					<img
						src={`${base}images/guides/sidebar-split.png`}
						width="312"
						height="980"
						alt="The Live sidebar in the split layout, with an icon bar beside the accounts panel"
					/>
					<figcaption>Split</figcaption>
				</figure>
				<figure>
					<img
						src={`${base}images/guides/sidebar-standard.png`}
						width="325"
						height="980"
						alt="The Live sidebar in the standard layout, with text navigation links above the accounts"
					/>
					<figcaption>Standard</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Check an account</h2>
			<p>
				Rest the pointer on an account for a moment to see its 30-day balance trend, cleared and
				uncleared amounts, and any upcoming scheduled transactions.
			</p>
			<div class="docs__stage docs__stage--card">
			<img
				src={`${base}images/guides/sidebar-hover.png`}
				width="292"
				height="265"
				alt="An account's hover card with a 30-day balance chart and its cleared and uncleared amounts"
			/>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Rename or close an account</h2>
			<p>
				Double-click an account to rename it. Right-click it for <strong>Rename</strong> and
				<strong>Close account</strong>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Collapse the sidebar</h2>
			<p>
				The button at the bottom folds the sidebar down to a rail of account tiles. Hover a tile to
				see the account's name.
			</p>
			<div class="docs__stage docs__stage--rail">
				<img
					src={`${base}images/guides/sidebar-rail.png`}
					width="640"
					height="830"
					alt="The collapsed rail, with an open Credit Cards folder and closed Savings and Retirement folders shown as small grids of icons"
				/>
			</div>
			<p>
				Each account group is a folder on the rail. Click the folder icon above an open group to
				close it into a grid of its first four accounts, and click the grid to open it again. Closing
				a folder also collapses that group in the full sidebar.
			</p>
		</section>
	</main>
</Base>
